From cfa9f01c5dfcb394ea2eb97c348a4d7cee78710c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Merlin Kooshmanian <mkooshmanian@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:12:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/33] sched/tgbs: support per-CPU runtime overrides for task
 groups

Adapt Yuri Andriaccio's per-CPU bandwidth configuration work for HCBS
to TGBS. The per-CPU budget idea and default/override model come from
his work, which inspired this implementation.

Expose cpu.runtime_us as a cgroup v2 flat-keyed interface. Accept a
scalar or "default RUNTIME" to update the default budget, "CPU RUNTIME"
to set an override, and "CPU default" to remove it. Default updates
preserve existing overrides. Read back the default followed by explicit
CPU overrides.

Keep a common period and validate proposed budgets against per-CPU
hierarchical and root-domain bandwidth constraints before applying
them. Preserve configured overrides when CPUs become inactive or
leave the effective cpuset, applying zero runtime outside the active
server mask.

Account for overrides when determining active groups and recalculating
the existing uniform root reservation. Per-CPU automatic root budgets
remain a separate change.

Based-on-a-patch-by: Yuri Andriaccio yurand2000@gmail.com
